From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:31:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] style(kanban): keep kanban_sync_client.py at its 2000-line
 cap after the rebase [daveey]

Main's 654cf8c340d brought kanban_sync_client.py to 1999 lines, so this
PR's two-line wire wrap in push() pushed it to 2001 and failed the health
FILE_LINES cap. Join the wrap; no behaviour change.
---
 hermes_cli/kanban_sync_client.py | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hermes_cli/kanban_sync_client.py b/hermes_cli/kanban_sync_client.py
index ce29e38d9d..e257069dff 100644
--- a/hermes_cli/kanban_sync_client.py
+++ b/hermes_cli/kanban_sync_client.py
@@ -677,8 +677,7 @@ def push(conn: sqlite3.Connection, hub: Hub, board: str, gateway: str, *, primar
             break
         with write_txn(conn):
             from hermes_cli.kanban_terminal_guard import strip_stale_push  # no wake reopens a done card [daveey]
-            wire = [strip_stale_push(conn, translate(_full_row_if_unseen(conn, r), _next_hlc(conn, gateway)))
-                    for r in rows]
+            wire = [strip_stale_push(conn, translate(_full_row_if_unseen(conn, r), _next_hlc(conn, gateway))) for r in rows]
             parents = _unacked_parents(conn, rows, gateway)
             wire = [op for op, _tid in parents] + wire
         try:
